# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project uses [SemVer/semantic versioning](https://semver.org/).

Numbers with a "#" prefix refer to Issue and Pull Request numbers on the
ANMS GitHub page: https://github.com/NASA-AMMOS/anms.

## [Unreleased]

### Added
- Tag-based GHCR image publishing (#300)
- Improved initial default ADM load process with dedicated route (#323)
- REST API error handling improvements with correct HTTP status codes and dtnma-tools SQL concurrency fix (#322)
- `/version` REST API endpoint (#365)
- Toast notification system with persistent alerts (#366, #371)
- Multi-file ADM upload support (#371)
- ARI column in the builder table (#371)

### Changed
- Production configuration moved into Puppet module parameters (#328)
- ResourceCache replaced with LFU cache for improved memory management (#351)
- CI migrated to Podman v5 (#359)
- Complete Angular port of frontend UI, replacing Vue (#353):
  - Agents page with management dialog and CRUD operations
  - Build tab with ARI builder and "send to agents" functionality
  - Report viewing with new report route integration
  - Logout redirect, version number in header
  - Toastr notification service, locally sourced fonts
  - Node.js upgraded from v16 to v22
- PostgreSQL upgraded from v14 to v18 (#364)
- Enterprise SSL Proxy Certificate installation refactored to use parameterized source URL (#363)
- OpenSearch containers as replacement for legacy search backend (#367)
- Core routes cleanup and consolidation (#380)
- Container build size optimization (#374)
- Build tests now use ruff linter (#372)
- Smarter password generation in setup script to meet updated OpenSearch requirements (#379)

### Fixed
- OpenAPI definition for `/adms/` route corrected (#360)
- Hello test endpoint (#370)
- Bug in ARI builder (#371)
- UID values exceeding SYS_UID_MAX (#378)

---

## [3.0.0-pre-alpha-1] - 2025-12-19

### Added
- Internal ARI transcoder (`_ace_transcode`) with configurable profile, replacing external `aricodec` dependency (#295)
- Grafana upgrade to v12 with PostgreSQL internal database, consolidated dashboard/widget definitions via text provisioning (#282, #283)
- Infinity-datasource Grafana plugin with example panels
- Prototype Help page and 404 Not Found page handler in UI
- amp-manager status indicator on UI Status page
- Automatic GHCR image creation on tag events, supplementing formal releases

### Changed
- Core `/services` REST API now returns JSON instead of plain text
- Core REST API detects timeouts and resolves overloaded `status` variable conflicts
- Updated `btable` id for report headers (#277)
- Grafana authentication/demo websocket proxy configuration fixes
- Grafana database password moved to environment variable
- Default ADM initialization logic moved into transcoder service
- REFDA startup added to allow IPN-scheme managers full access

### Fixed
- Default database warning in Grafana
- Threading and database issues in internal transcoder
- GHCR image naming when triggered by tag

### Removed
- Services related to transcoder from default startup configuration

---

## [2.0.0] - 2025-10-30

### Added
- Light compose profile for reduced-footprint deployments (#205)
- Parallel light compose configuration (#196)
- GHCR container publishing pipeline (#251)
- Quickstart script for streamlined developer onboarding (#242)
- SonarQube/SonarCloud CI integration for static analysis (#208-#212, #244)
- Time-based rule and control creation in the build tab (#198)
- EDDS ARI selection on the build tab (#194)
- Manual refresh button on data tables, replacing unreliable auto-refresh (#197)
- CODEOWNERS file for automated PR review assignment (#195)
- CAMP repository migration groundwork (#191)

### Changed
- All npm packages updated to latest stable versions (#160)
- ARI display streamlined: reference parameters removed from display, compute logic simplified (#163)
- ACE and ADM updated to new bp-agent version (#165)
- ACE and ADM Dockerfiles renamed and restructured (#159)
- Podman support added alongside Docker (#178)
- Docker Compose configuration fixes and updates (#183)
- NGINX completely removed from the stack (#189)
- Unneeded core routes removed (#223)
- Unused SSL configuration removed (#221)
- Core route for translating and sending ARI consolidated into single endpoint (#204)
- Workflow CI jobs combined using matrix strategy (#234)
- ContainerFiles combined to eliminate intermediate images (#233)
- Dockerfiles migrated to common base image (#243)
- Submodules updated (#203, #249)
- Latest dtnma-tools and SQL schema adopted (#249)
- Environment variable override for amp-manager port restored (#257)
- CI image tags now use only safe characters (#124)
- Release script updated for public repository workflow

### Fixed
- CI deploy issues (#170)
- Puppet-lint CI and identified lint issues (#179)
- CI jobs stability (#230)
- Healthcheck SQL role restored (#229)
- Correlator nonce misbehavior - duplicate nonce generation resolved (#232)
- YANG file upload failures (#236)
- Bad input handling on ADM routes (#256)
- Transcoder log table navigation misbehavior (#260)
- Ping output suppressed from anms-core status page to reduce log noise (#262)
- Invalid use of ARI text prefix for binary form of values (#269)
- Dependency upgrades addressing Dependabot critical and high alerts (#136, #137, #157, #158, #162, #273)
- Built-image tag and base-image qualified name fixes (#276)

---

## [1.1.0] - 2024-08-26

### Added
- Agent details modal (#64)
- Agent management modal with full CRUD (#78)
- Received reports display with missing reports support (#72)
- Report generation and report displays in the build tab (#120)
- State-based rule and control creation (#122)
- Navigation filtering on the exploration build tab (#5, #88, #123)
- GitLab CI pipeline (#6)
- Puppet-lint SARIF reporting for code scanning (#75)
- PKIX certificate installation in CI and deployment (#80)

### Changed
- Build script updated for image tar release
- RHEL version updated for AMMOS compatibility (#67)
- CI jobs relocated (#70)
- Manual docker-compose package install in Puppet (#76)
- ION switched to dtnma-tools backend (#79)
- Latest dtnma-tools main branch adopted (#83)
- Latest ION submodule for TV fix (#101)

### Fixed
- Overly permissive regular expression range - security fix (#63)
- Rate limiters added to GET requests and routes, resolving code scanning issues (#62)
- ION NM failure on hex strings containing blank spaces (#69)
- Received reports: max vector limit in ION avoided, table reload fixed, dead code removed (#72)
- Report database: agent parameter handling corrected, UI rule generation fixes (#82)
- Footer formatting overflow when content exceeds viewport (#102)

---

## [1.0.0] - 2023-08-31

### Added
- Initial public release of ANMS v1.0, imported from private source repository

---

## [0.2.0] - 2022-06-10

### Added
- Build tab, which allows for building of ARIs
- anms-core, centralized orchestration component which now all ANMS-developed components will use to retrieve data from other components
- REST API documentation websites for anms-core in both OpenAPI (at /docs) and Redoc (at /redoc) formats
- Initial unit testing for anms-core and anms-ui
- All components now support PostgreSQL and MySQL databases, with notional support for MariaDB.

### Changed
- anms-ui now makes no direct db requests, they all are directed through anms-core
- Grafana now uses proxy authentication with nginx to secure all panels (visible inside of the monitor tab)
- Removed unsupported/non-functional UI components including Networking and Alerts tabs
- Fixed hard-coded and permanent admin and user accounts for UI, now only an admin is created on installation and can be disabled
- Fixed password complexity validation issues with UI
- Updated build.sh, configuration, and docker-compose files to support remote server deployment
- Updated Agents table and initial Agent pages to move away from use of Grafana for simple CRUD operations
- Removed incomplete user invitation system in lieu of server admin user account management
- Initial REST API role-based access controls for user management endpoint

## [0.1.1] - 2022-03-09

### Added
- Grafana panels and documentation for viewing report variables
- Interface to help construct controls that set up TBRs for agents to send reports at intervals

### Changed
- Updated versions of npm module dependencies per vulnerability analysis
- Fixed issues related to adding users

## [0.0.1] - 2022-02-08

### Added
- Initial Release
